# Keep the proven level

Done means the proofs still pass after the latest edit, not that they passed once.

- After any change under `sql/`, run every `sql/prove_*.sql` the change can affect, including earlier facts this change sits on. A kernel change re-runs `sql/prove.sql` and every later proof.
- A vector found later is added to the permanent proof and re-run. A one-off script does not count, and it does not excuse moving on.
- Do not delete, comment out, or narrow an assertion to make a script pass. Restore the guarantee and re-run.
- Do not add a fact or behavior that leaves an older proof unexecutable or leaves a known hole in place.
- A skipped run, a happy-path-only script, or a green run from before the latest edit is not the current level.

```text
BAD: edit the payout trigger, re-run prove_payout.sql only, leave prove_statement.sql stale
GOOD: edit the payout trigger, re-run prove_payout.sql and prove_statement.sql, both exit 0, then stop
```
